@page "/component-owned-scope"
@rendermode @(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))

<PageTitle>Component-owned scope</PageTitle>

<h1>Component-owned scope</h1>

<p class="lead">
    This page keeps using the same scoped <code>IScopedUserService</code> that directly injects
    <code>AppDbContext</code>. The difference is that each card owns its own DI scope, so each card gets its own
    scoped service instance and its own scoped <code>DbContext</code>.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-primary" role="alert">
    Expected result: all cards should succeed, and the service IDs and DbContext IDs should differ between cards because
    each component has its own scope.
</div>

<div class="card border-primary shadow-sm mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4">Why this is safe</h2>
        <p>
            In normal Blazor Server behavior, scoped services are shared across the whole circuit. By switching each
            child component to an owned scope, the scoped service stops being circuit-wide for that component and becomes
            <strong>component-local</strong> instead.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
            That means the service can still directly inject <code>AppDbContext</code>, but the injected context is no
            longer shared across sibling components. The components can all load concurrently because they no longer
            compete for one shared context instance.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-xl-3 g-4">
    <div class="col">
        <OwnedScopeUserLookupCard Title="Component A" UserId="1" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <OwnedScopeUserLookupCard Title="Component B" UserId="2" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <OwnedScopeUserLookupCard Title="Component C" UserId="3" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <OwnedScopeUserLookupCard Title="Component D" UserId="4" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <OwnedScopeUserLookupCard Title="Component E" UserId="5" />
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <OwnedScopeUserLookupCard Title="Component F" UserId="6" />
    </div>
</div>
